-- title:
--   Raw Whittaker bundle over ℚ and unramified laws
-- statement:
--   Fix a Hecke eigensystem $\Theta$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with complex values (a non-zero ideal $\Theta.\mathrm{level}$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with families $\Theta.a,\Theta.b$ indexed by the finite places), a homomorphism $\xi$ from the central subgroup of `productionPinsGeneral ℚ` to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, finite sets $S_0\subseteq S$ of height-one primes such that no $v\notin S$ divides $\Theta.\mathrm{level}$, and $\varphi_0:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})\to\mathbb{C}$ which is non-zero and an isotypic cusp form at these pins for $\xi$, level $\Theta.\mathrm{level}$, bad set $S_0$ and $\Theta$ (smooth cuspidal automorphy, continuity, invariance under the level subgroup, the Hecke coset eigenvalue $\Theta.a\,v$ and the central eigenvalue $(\mathrm{cNorm}\,v)^{-1}\Theta.b\,v$ for $v\notin S_0$). Assume further: at each prime $p$ the local Whittaker space `localSpaceAt` of $\varphi_0$ for `psiQ` is generated by any of its non-zero vectors under right translation, has finite-dimensional spaces of invariants under each open subgroup, and consists of vectors invariant under some open subgroup; $\varphi_0$ is reproduced by right convolution with a factorisable test function; $\varphi_0$ satisfies the predicate `HasArchCharacterAt₀` for `archWeightCharAt … n` at the real place for some $n\in\mathbb{Z}$; the first Whittaker coefficient of $\varphi_0$ factorises as $W_{A,0}(\mathrm{ratArchGL2}\,g)\cdot W_{f,0}(\mathrm{finFactor}\,g)$, with $W_{A,0}$ not identically zero and $W_{f,0}(1)\neq 0$; and a family $\varpi_v$ of elements of the valuation rings with valuation $\exp(-1)$ and non-zero image in each completion. The conclusion is a conjunction of four blocks. First, the invariant bundle: $\varphi_0$ is continuous; it is a cuspidal automorphic function at the pins for $\xi$; it is a finite linear combination $\varphi_0(x)=\sum_{i<m}c_i\varphi_0(xg_i)$ of its own right translates by elements $g_i$ of the finite-adelic subgroup; $\varphi_0(zg)=\xi(z)\varphi_0(g)$ for every idele class unit $z$ acting by the central scalar, $\xi$ being read through the identification of the unit group with the top subgroup; the zeroth Whittaker coefficient vanishes identically; for each $g$ the family of norms of the Whittaker coefficients indexed by $a\in\mathbb{Q}$ is summable; the assumed factorisation of the first coefficient holds; $W_{f,0}$ is measurable, has $\lvert W_{f,0}\rvert$ invariant under left translation by the finite unipotent subgroup, and is right invariant under some open subgroup; at each finite $v$ there is a unitary additive character $\psi$ of the completion, trivial on the integers and non-trivial on some $r/\varpi_v$, with $W_{f,0}(\mathrm{finFactor}(\mathrm{placeEmbed}\,v\,(\mathrm{unipotent}\,x)\cdot g))=\psi(x)W_{f,0}(\mathrm{finFactor}\,g)$; for each $p$ and each $g$ trivial at $p$ the slice $h\mapsto W_{f,0}(\mathrm{finFactor}(g\cdot\mathrm{placeEmbed}\,p\,h))$ lies in the local Whittaker space at $p$; $\varphi_0$ is right invariant under some open subgroup of the finite-adelic subgroup; the archimedean weight condition holds for some $n$; and every Whittaker coefficient integral converges absolutely. Second, the unramified laws off $S$: for $v\notin S$, $W_{f,0}\circ\mathrm{finFactor}$ is right invariant under `localLevelOne` at $v$ for the unit ideal and under unipotents with integral entry; there are $b_i$ in the valuation ring, indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,(\mathrm{absNorm}\,v)$, with $\sum_i W_{f,0}(g\cdot\mathrm{repSome}(\varpi_v,b_i))+W_{f,0}(g\cdot\mathrm{repInf}(\varpi_v))=\Theta.a\,v\cdot W_{f,0}(g)$ after applying $\mathrm{finFactor}$; and $W_{f,0}(g\cdot\mathrm{scalarPi}(\varpi_v))=(\Theta.b\,v/\mathrm{absNorm}\,v)W_{f,0}(g)$ likewise. Third, at every prime $p$, $W_{f,0}\circ\mathrm{finFactor}$ is right invariant under `localLevelOne` at $p$ for the ideal $\Theta.\mathrm{level}$. Fourth, $W_{f,0}(1)\neq 0$.
--
--   This packages the analytic and Hecke-theoretic properties of an isotypic cusp form over $\mathbb{Q}$ and of the finite part of its first Whittaker coefficient into the single invariant bundle on which the shaping induction for the finite Whittaker function operates, including the unramified Hecke and central relations with the eigensystem $\Theta$ outside $S$. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_shapedRaw_bundle_forall_shellSupport_transl_rat`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_shapedRaw_bundle_forall_shellSupport_transl_rat).
